Draw a shadow for the shadowed toolbar button effect

The toolbar button effect holds three entries. The plain entry gives the
general button effect, and the two other entries name the etch and the
shadow. The style reads that option at one place, and the place tests the
etch alone. The shadowed entry therefore reaches the same code as the
plain entry, and it moves no pixel of any configuration.

The bevel paint now takes the effect of the widget, and gives drawEtch() a
raised edge for the shadow. A toolbar button takes the toolbar button
effect, and every other widget takes the general button effect. The
decision leaves drawEtch(), because the caller holds the sunken state that
a shadow needs. A pressed toolbar button therefore keeps its etch, as the
general button paint demands.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 3 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
index 46465139..1390dab5 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
@@ -2032,7 +2032,14 @@ Style::drawLightBevelReal(QPainter *p, const QRect &rOrig,
             drawGlow(p, rOrig, WIDGET_DEF_BUTTON==w && option->state&State_MouseOver ? WIDGET_STD_BUTTON : w,
                      glowFocus ? m_focusCols : 0L);
         else
-            drawEtch(p, rOrig, widget, w, EFFECT_SHADOW==opts.buttonEffect && WIDGET_BUTTON(w) && !sunken);
+        {
+            // A toolbar button takes its own effect, and the plain entry of
+            // that effect gives the general button effect.
+            EEffect effect(WIDGET_TOOLBAR_BUTTON==w && EFFECT_NONE!=opts.tbarBtnEffect
+                           ? opts.tbarBtnEffect : opts.buttonEffect);
+
+            drawEtch(p, rOrig, widget, w, EFFECT_SHADOW==effect && WIDGET_BUTTON(w) && !sunken);
+        }
     }
 
     if(doBorder)
@@ -2098,9 +2105,6 @@ void Style::drawEtch(QPainter *p, const QRect &r, const QWidget *widget,  EWidge
         br;
     QColor       col(Qt::black);
 
-    if(WIDGET_TOOLBAR_BUTTON==w && EFFECT_ETCH==opts.tbarBtnEffect)
-        raised=false;
-
     buildSplitPath(r, round, qtcGetRadius(&opts, r.width(), r.height(), w, RADIUS_ETCH), tl, br);
 
     col.setAlphaF(USE_CUSTOM_ALPHAS(opts) ? opts.customAlphas[ALPHA_ETCH_DARK] : ETCH_TOP_ALPHA);
